## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical batch ingestion, per-record contracts, privacy masking, and idempotent upserts in a common lakehouse pattern.

## Key Concepts

- Data contracts, masking, bad_data routing
- Iceberg schema evolution, upserts, unique keys
- Test plans for duplicates, new fields, and schema drift

## Code Example

```javascript
function validate(record) {
  const required = ["user_id","event_ts","event_type"];
  for (const k of required) if (!(k in record)) return false;
  // simple mask
  if (record.payload) record.payload.pii = null;
  return true;
}
```

```javascript
// MERGE-like upsert (pseudocode)
MERGE INTO iceberg.fact AS t
USING staging AS s
ON t.user_id = s.user_id AND t.event_ts = s.event_ts
WHEN MATCHED THEN UPDATE SET ...
WHEN NOT MATCHED THEN INSERT ...
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical data quality, late data handling, and observability in a real-world lakehouse pipeline.

## Key Concepts
- Per-record contracts and simple validator logic
- Upserts into Iceberg star schema with deduplication by event_id
- Late data handling with watermarking (15 minutes)
- Lightweight observability: lineage, conforming vs non-conforming counts, metrics sink
- Trade-offs: Spark Structured Streaming vs Flink for beginner workloads

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo validator
function validate(record) {
  if (!record.event_id || !record.ts || !record.device_id) return false;
  if (typeof record.metrics?.value !== 'number') return false;
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you design the bad_data retention and purge policy?
- Which metrics would you expose to operators for quick health checks?

## Why This Is Asked
Probes privacy-preserving multi-tenant data architectures, lineage, and streaming trade-offs not covered by earlier questions.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant isolation
- Data contracts and schema drift
- Dynamic masking of PII
- GDPR delete and lineage preservation
- Iceberg lakehouse semantics
- Spark vs Flink trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: mask PII fields for non-admins
function maskPII(record, role) {
  if (role !== 'admin') {
    record.email = '***@***';
    record.phone = record.phone?.replace(/\\d/g, 'x');
  }
  return record;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate per-tenant deletes across long-running streams?
- How would you test schema drift and masking policy changes in production?
